invariant: INV-16
file: ct.h
catches: test/x25519-builds.sh
reason: X25519=wide stops needing CH_NATIVE_MUL128, so a build selects the
  radix-2^51 field and nobody states that the 64x64->128 multiply it runs
  every product on takes the same time for every operand. The
  architectures do not promise that, which is why Arm publishes FEAT_DIT
  and Intel its DOIT list, and CH_NATIVE_WIDEMUL cannot stand in because
  it names another instruction. Every source still compiles and every
  vector passes, so the compiler's refusal is the only check.

--- old
#ifndef CH_NATIVE_MUL128
#error "X25519=wide needs -DCH_NATIVE_MUL128: the build asserts the 64x64->128 multiply's timing"
#endif
--- new
